      "content": "I'm not a doctor, but I can provide some general guidance. Taking dextromethorphan with Zoloft (sertraline) may not be the best option, as dextromethorphan can interact with certain antidepressants, including SSRIs like Zoloft. However, Robitussin DM or similar products containing dextromethorphan and a coumarin-based cough suppressant may be available over-the-counter. You may want to consider an alternative, such as an antacids or an expectorant, or consult your doctor or pharmacist for personalized advice.",
